# Part Seven — Cases and Case Studies

> Court judgements, incidents and the three syllabus case studies. Use one case per answer to make an argument concrete.

## 7.1  Court judgements

::: table | Court judgements on women's rights.
@widths 1.6,3.8,6.6,2
@font 9.5
Year | Case | What it decided | Topic
1967 | *Khurshid Bibi v. Muhammad Amin* (Supreme Court) | Recognised the wife's right to *khula* | T5
1997 / 2004 | *Saima Waheed* (Lahore High Court; Supreme Court) | An adult Muslim woman may marry without her guardian's consent | T5, T7
2009 | *Dr Muhammad Aslam Khaki* (Supreme Court) | Recognised *khawaja siras*; third-gender identity cards | T1
2011 | Mukhtaran Mai appeal (Supreme Court, 21 April) | Upheld acquittal of five accused; one life sentence | T7
2012 | Lady Health Workers (Supreme Court) | Regularisation of LHWs | T5
2021 | Federal Shariat Court on child marriage | A minimum marriage age is not against Islam | T5
2022 | Qandeel Baloch appeal (Lahore High Court) | Brother acquitted after parental pardon | T7
2023 | Federal Shariat Court on the Transgender Act | Key sections held repugnant; appeal pending in 2026 | T1
2025 | Noor Mukadam appeal (Supreme Court, May) | Upheld Zahir Jaffer's death sentence for murder | T7
:::

## 7.2  Incidents that changed the debate

::: table | Incidents and their consequences.
@widths 1.6,3.8,6.6,2
@font 9.5
Year | Incident | Consequence | Topic
1983 | Safia Bibi case | Blind girl convicted of *zina* after reporting rape; national outcry | T3
1999 | Samia Sarwar killed in her lawyers' office | International attention to honour killing | T7
2002 | Mukhtaran Mai gang-raped (Meerwala, 22 June) | Debate leading to the 2006 Act | T7
2012 | Ali Enterprises factory fire, Karachi | About 260 deaths; global supply-chain debate | T4
2012 | Malala shot (Mingora, 9 October) | Global campaign for girls' education | T7
2013 | Rana Plaza collapse, Bangladesh | More than 1,100 deaths; Bangladesh Accord | T4
2014 | Saba Qaiser shot and survived (Gujranwala) | *A Girl in the River*; 2016 honour law | T7
2016 | Qandeel Baloch killed (Multan, July) | Honour-killing Act passed in October | T7
2018 | Zainab Ansari murdered (Kasur, January) | Zainab Alert Act 2020 | T7
2020 | Motorway gang rape (September) | Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act 2021 | T7
2021 | Noor Mukadam murdered (Islamabad, July) | Death sentence upheld (2025) | T7
2022 | Floods | About 33 million affected; 650,000 pregnant women | T4, T5
2025 | Sana Yousaf killed (Islamabad, 2 June) | Debate on online visibility and entitlement | T7
2025 | Bano Satakzai and Ehsanullah Samalani killed (Degari) | Viral video forced arrests | T7
:::

## 7.3  The three syllabus case studies

::: table | The three case studies in one table.
@widths 2.6,3.8,3.8,3.8
@font 9
Aspect | Mukhtaran Mai | Malala Yousafzai | Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy
Born / place | Meerwala, Muzaffargarh, South Punjab (MCQ 2016) | 12 July 1997, Mingora, Swat (MCQ 2016) | 1978, Karachi
Key event | Gang rape on a *panchayat*'s order, 22 June 2002 | Shot by the Taliban, 9 October 2012 | Oscars for *Saving Face* (2012) and *A Girl in the River* (2016)
Legal journey or work | ATC 2002 (6 death sentences); LHC 2005; SC 2011 (one life sentence) | BBC diary 2009; UN speech 12 July 2013; Malala Fund 2013 | Acid attacks; honour killing (Saba Qaiser)
Recognition | *Glamour* Woman of the Year (2005); memoir 2006 | Nobel Peace Prize 2014 (aged 17, with Kailash Satyarthi) | Hilal-i-Imtiaz (2012); TIME 100; Emmys
Impact | Girls' school in Meerwala; women's welfare organisation | Global agenda on girls' education; about $14.6m invested in Pakistan | Acid Act 2011; honour-killing Act 2016
Criticism | State worried about its "image" | "Western agent"; "I am not Malala" day (2014) | "Defaming Pakistan abroad"
Asked in | 2019 (with structural and direct violence) | 2025 (achievements, local and global) | 2020 (background of the two documentaries)
:::
